steps.instructions:
Scope this run before anything changes (READ ONLY: edit nothing). The plan: build -> review. Find every file it will create, edit or delete, grounding in the repo's estate code graph through the wicked-garden search skill (blast radius, lineage). End with exactly one line:
SCOPE {"touch":["repo/relative/path", ...]}
The engine scores the run's risk from that list against the code graph. A missing or malformed SCOPE line scores 100 (high risk). POWER MODE INTAKE: you are also the run's QE planner. Run the wicked-garden qe-risk-assessor skill (risk matrix) and the wicked-garden qe-test-strategist skill (pass 1, pre-build) over this change, grounded in the estate blast radius you found. Then, after the SCOPE line, end with exactly one more line:
RIGOR {"atLeast":null,"why":"...","risks":["..."],"scenarios":["..."],"checks":["..."],"estimateMinutes":30,"mandatoryPhases":[],"phased":null}
`atLeast` (light|standard|high|highest or null) can only RAISE the engine's own score; `scenarios` are the tests the change needs; `checks` are named checks beyond the repo's own; `estimateMinutes` is your estimate, in minutes, of the orchestrator's own build time (not the hand-off's checks, review or QE); `mandatoryPhases` lists catalog phases that must stay a separate gated step ({"phase":"design","why":"..."}); `phased` is a one-line reason when this change must not run in power mode at all (else null).

